{"_id":"68a7360a8ec3d8323af114a0","nodeId":"cXVy1lx2XqY_j8gxz-y60","roadmapSlug":"angular","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:50.309Z","description":"# Testing component bindings\n\nAngular processes all data bindings once for each JavaScript event cycle, from the root of the application component tree through all child components. Data binding plays an important role in communication between a template and its component, and is also important for communication between parent and child components.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Component","url":"https://angular.dev/guide/components","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e23"},{"type":"official","title":"Basics of Testing Components","url":"https://angular.io/guide/testing-components-basics","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e24"},{"type":"official","title":"Component Testing Scenarios ΓÇó Angular","url":"https://angular.dev/guide/testing/components-scenarios","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e25"},{"type":"feed","title":"Explore top posts about Testing","url":"https://app.daily.dev/tags/testing?ref=roadmapsh","_id":"6a7f49d1cb44947debcf0e26"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:01:05.151Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/angular/content/cXVy1lx2XqY_j8gxz-y60.md"}